import { PLAY_H, PLAY_W, TILE } from '..[elided private context: 20 bytes, sha256:dd41dbdce37be7da66b741ac31ccee269bd11f2093aa3021083e78d056caaeed]';

const CODE: Record<string, keyof Input> = { u: 'up', d: 'down', l: 'left', r: 'right', a: 'attack', s: 'start' };

/** Same token format as tests/scripts/playthrough.ts ('u12' = hold up 12 frames). */
export function decode(script: string): ScriptStep[] {
  return script.trim().split(/\s+/).map((token) => {
    const m = /^([udlras]*|\.)(\d+)$/.exec(token);
    if (!m) throw new Error(`bad token ${token}`);
    const input: Partial<Input> = {};
    for (const ch of m[1] ?? '') {
      const key = CODE[ch];
      if (key) input[key] = true;
    }
    return { frames: Number(m[2]), input };
  });
}

/** The shipped game, already playing at the start position. */
export function realState(seed = 1): GameState {
  const s = createState(content, seed);
  newGame(s);
  return s;
}

export function hold(state: GameState, input: Partial<Input>, frames: number): void {
  for (let i = 0; i < frames; i++) step(state, { ...NONE, ...input });
}

/** Hold `input` until `pred` is true or `max` frames pass; returns frames used (-1 if never). */
export function holdUntil(state: GameState, input: Partial<Input>, pred: (s: GameState) => boolean, max: number): number {
  for (let i = 0; i < max; i++) {
    step(state, { ...NONE, ...input });
    if (pred(state)) return i + 1;
  }
  return -1;
}

/** Run a decoded script until `pred` fires; returns the frame index at which it fired, or -1. */
export function runUntil(state: GameState, steps: readonly ScriptStep[], pred: (s: GameState) => boolean): number {
  let f = 0;
  for (const s of steps) {
    for (let i = 0; i < s.frames; i++) {
      step(state, { ...NONE, ...s.input });
      f++;
      if (pred(state)) return f;
    }
  }
  return -1;
}

export function body(state: GameState): Rect {
  return rectOf(state.player, state.player.box);
}

/** Tile indices overlapped by the half-open span [a, a + len). */
function span(a: number, len: number): [number, number] {
  return [Math.floor(a / TILE), Math.ceil((a + len) / TILE) - 1];
}

/** Every tile the player's body currently overlaps that it may not stand on (out of bounds counts). */
export function solidUnderBody(state: GameState): { col: number; row: number }[] {
  const b = body(state);
  const out: { col: number; row: number }[] = [];
  const [c0, c1] = span(b.x, b.w);
  const [r0, r1] = span(b.y, b.h);
  for (let r = r0; r <= r1; r++) {
    for (let c = c0; c <= c1; c++) {
      if (!isPassable(state, c, r, false)) out.push({ col: c, row: r });
    }
  }
  return out;
}

export function bodyInsideField(state: GameState): boolean {
  const b = body(state);
  return b.x >= 0 && b.y >= 0 && b.x + b.w <= PLAY_W && b.y + b.h <= PLAY_H;
}

export function finite(...ns: number[]): boolean {
  return ns.every((n) => Number.isFinite(n));
}

export function enemiesOf(state: GameState): Enemy[] {
  return state.room.entities.filter((e): e is Enemy => e.kind === 'enemy');
}

export function pickupsOf(state: GameState): Pickup[] {
  return state.room.entities.filter((e): e is Pickup => e.kind === 'pickup');
}

export function projectilesOf(state: GameState): Projectile[] {
  return state.room.entities.filter((e): e is Projectile => e.kind === 'projectile');
}

export function tileChar(state: GameState, col: number, row: number): string | undefined {
  return tileAt(state.room, col, row);
}

/** JSON of the state minus the immutable content bundle (ARCHITECTURE.md §5). */
export function strip(state: GameState): string {
  return JSON.stringify({ ...state, content: undefined });
}

/** A tiny deterministic LCG for generating input scripts (not the game's RNG). */
export function lcg(seed: number): () => number {
  let s = seed >>> 0;
  return () => {
    s = (Math.imul(s, 1664525) + 1013904223) >>> 0;
    return s / 0x100000000;
  };
}

export function randomInput(next: () => number): Partial<Input> {
  const r = next();
  const input: Partial<Input> = {};
  if (r < 0.2) input.up = true;
  else if (r < 0.4) input.down = true;
  else if (r < 0.6) input.left = true;
  else if (r < 0.8) input.right = true;
  if (next() < 0.15) input.attack = true;
  if (next() < 0.01) input.start = true;
  return input;
}
